course: dictionary
lesson: 5037
title: Injure and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To injure someone means to hurt them, so that part of their body is damaged. You can find the meaning by reading the words around it. «In tackle football players wear a helmet, because tackling with the head down can injure the neck.» Helmets are worn to keep you safe, so injure must mean hurt, and the neck is the part that gets damaged.
explain: Try the swap test. Put «hurt» in place of «injure»: «tackling with the head down can hurt the neck». It still makes sense, so hurt is a good meaning. Always check your meaning by trying it in the sentence.
explain: Injure can also mean to upset someone's feelings or pride. Read this sentence: «Her unkind words injured his pride.» Nobody's skin is broken here. The words hurt his pride, so they upset him. Context tells you which meaning is right.
fact: Injure is a verb: injure, injures, injured, injuring.
fact: «Injure» means to hurt a person or an animal so that part of the body is damaged.
fact: «Injured» tells the reader that someone was hurt, as in «seriously injured» or «injured in an accident».
fact: To injure someone's feelings or pride means to upset them.
fact: You can say «injure yourself» when you hurt your own body by accident.
exercise: «On ice you never throw snowballs at faces, because they can injure eyes.» What does injure mean here? | Cover with snow | Shine brightly | *Hurt, so that the eyes get damaged | Make a loud noise
exercise: Find and copy the word that tells us someone was hurt: «A girl of eight in Canada rode in the front seat; in a small crash the airbag burst out and injured her neck.» | front | crash | airbag | *injured
exercise: A friend says, «That mean joke injured Sam's pride.» What does this mean? | It made Sam taller | It made Sam laugh loudly | It fixed Sam's bike | *It upset Sam
test: «At a firework display, stand behind the barrier, because fireworks can burn and injure people who are too close.» Why must people stand behind the barrier? | To hear the bangs more clearly | *To stay safe from being hurt | To get a better view of the sky | To make the fireworks go faster
test: Which word has a similar meaning to injure, when we mean hurt? | Tickle | *Harm | Lift | Wash
exam: Which sentence uses injure to mean upset someone's feelings? | He injured his knee falling off the wall. | The fall could injure your neck. | *Her unkind words injured his pride. | The strong wind injured the tree.
